### iOS App Store Release Checklist

- [ ] Apple ID with 2FA enabled  
- [ ] Join Apple Developer Program ($99/year)  
- [ ] Use Xcode/EAS to build signed `.ipa` or `.app`  
- [x] Ensure app conforms to [App Store Review Guidelines]   
- [x] Prepare metadata in App Store Connect:  
  - App Name, Subtitle, Keywords, Categories  
  - Description, Support URL, Marketing URL, Copyright  
  - Privacy Policy URL and App Privacy details   
  - Age Rating, Content Rights, Demo/test account credentials  
- [ ] Create screenshots and optional preview video (various device sizes)   
- [ ] Use TestFlight for beta testing with sandbox users   
- [ ] Archive and upload build via Xcode or EAS Submit  
- [ ] Attach build to version in App Store Connect  
- [ ] Provide App Review notes (especially for special features/external links)   
- [ ] Submit for review  
- [ ] Choose release type (Manual/Automatic/Scheduled)  
- [ ] After approval: Release in App Store Connect  
- [ ] Post-launch: Monitor analytics, crash logs, and reviews

### Android Google Play Release Checklist

- [ ] Google Play Developer account created ($25 one-time fee)   
- [ ] Ensure app adheres to Play Program Policies & DDA   
- [ ] Build a release-ready Android App Bundle (`.aab`), minSdk version, no debug flags   
- [ ] Sign the AAB correctly  
- [ ] Prepare Play Console store listing:  
  - Title (≤50 chars), Short Description (≤80), Full Description (≤4,000)   
  - App icon (512×512), Feature Graphic (1024×500), Screenshots *(min 2)*   
  - Optional promo video (YouTube, first 30 s play)   
  - Privacy Policy URL and contact info   
  - Content rating questionnaire, pricing & distribution regions (incl. Brazil/EU)   
- [ ] Create in-app products or subscriptions (link Merchant Account)   
- [ ] Use testing tracks:  
  - Internal (team)  
  - Closed beta (limited testers)  
  - Open beta (public)   
- [ ] Upload AAB and release notes under **Release > Production** (or beta)   
- [ ] Review release summary and artifacts  
- [ ] Submit for review (takes 2–7 days)   
- [ ] Post-launch: monitor downloads, crashes (Play Console & Firebase), reviews, revenue   


